    "title": "Rohit Sharma Equals David Warner's World Record Of Most... | Cricket News - News18",
    "text": "Rohit, who is the world’s No. 1 ODI batter, faced a total of 94 balls on Wednesday and, with the help of 18 fours and 9 sixes, scored 155 runs. By playing a knock of 155 runs in Mumbai’s 8-wicket win, Rohit equalled David Warner’s world record of most 150+ scores in List A cricket. Warner played 210 List A matches from 2007 to 2023 and scored 8886 runs. He registered scores of 150+ nine times in the 50-over format of the game, and now Rohit also has nine 150+ scores to his credit. Rohit has crossed the 150-run mark eight times in 279 ODI matches for India and one time in the Vijay Hazare Trophy as a Mumbai player. Rohit Sharma’s 150+ scores in List A Cricket During his 14-year-long ODI career for Australia from 2009 to 2023, Warner played 161 ODIs and registered seven scores of 150+. His other two 150+ scores in List A matches came while representing New South Wales.",
